hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1290","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: My father and I were sitting on the road and he would show me the Qur’an. And I turned to him. He said: So he recited the prostration and prostrated, so I said to him: Do you prostrate on the road? He said: Yes, I heard Abu Dharr say: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Which mosque was built on earth first? He said: “The Grand Mosque.” He said: I said: Then what? He said: “Then Al-Aqsa Mosque.” He said: I said: Then what? He said: “Then Al-Aqsa Mosque.” He said: I said: How much time was there between them? He said: “Forty years,” then he said: “Wherever prayer leads you to pray, that is a mosque.”"
